  "description": "TOHWUL crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H64 Co4 N50 O50 Tm8 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),8(C1 H4 O1),14(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tm1 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 9 O neighbors; Tm4 (Tm) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Tm5 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm6 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm7 (Tm) has 9 O neighbors; Tm8 (Tm) has 9 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.617-4.010 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.75-116.15°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tm(pyzic){Tm3Co2(pyzha)6(*pyzha)(NO3)2(H2O)(MeOH)2}]2·(NO3)2·nH2O·8MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
